.TH BLK_MONITOR 1 "2026-06-23" "blk_monitor 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blk_monitor \- report when observed block-device I/O has been idle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blk_monitor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I /dev/DEVICE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blk_monitor
samples Linux block statistics and exits after a configurable period with no
observed I/O activity.
By default it calls
.BR sync (2)
after the idle threshold is reached.
.PP
The program does not unmount filesystems, eject media, or power off hardware.
An idle result is not a safe-removal guarantee.
Unmount or eject the device before physically disconnecting it.
.PP
Partitions are resolved to their parent block device through
.IR /sys/class/block .
The parser supports legacy statistics and optional discard and flush fields.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISEC\fR
Poll interval in seconds. Range: 1\(en60. Default: 2.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-idle\-time " " \fISEC\fR
Required consecutive observed idle time. Range: 5\(en3600. Default: 10.
The reported duration may exceed this value by less than one poll interval.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sync
Call the system-wide
.BR sync (2)
function after reaching the idle threshold. This is the default.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-no\-sync
Do not call
.BR sync (2).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress samples and print exactly one final status line.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print one status line per poll.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print one JSON object per poll and a final idle event after any requested
.BR sync (2)
has completed.
The final object includes
.IR sync_performed ,
.I sync_scope
set to
.IR system ,
and
.I unmount_performed
set to
.IR false .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors.
Colors are also disabled when stdout is not a terminal or
.B NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The observed I/O-idle threshold was reached.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid input, unavailable or malformed statistics, or output failure.
.TP
.B 2
Interrupted by
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
before reaching the threshold.
.SH SAFETY AND PRIVILEGES
Monitoring and
.BR sync (2)
do not require root.
Do not grant this program
.BR CAP_SYS_ADMIN .
.PP
.BR sync (2)
flushes all mounted filesystems and does not unmount the monitored device.
Other processes can issue new writes after the idle result.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Monitor a whole device:
.RS 4
.nf
blk_monitor /dev/sdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Monitor a partition through its parent device:
.RS 4
.nf
blk_monitor -i 1 -t 5 /dev/nvme0n1p2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream JSON without running
.BR sync (2):
.RS 4
.nf
blk_monitor --json --no-sync /dev/sdb | jq -c .
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/block/<device>
Used to resolve partitions to parent devices.
.TP
.I /sys/block/<device>/stat
Kernel block statistics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sync (2),
.BR sync (8),
.BR umount (8),
.BR udisksctl (1),
.BR losetup (8)
